1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:13,237
In this video you will learn how payments work in NTSOne: how to switch them on, how
the payment fund works, and how to withdraw your money. The amounts you will see are
sample demonstration data.

2
00:00:13,837 --> 00:00:29,499
Open a program, an order form or a poll, and find the Payments section. Switch on Take
payments and set what each thing costs, such as a registration fee. People then pay
with Orange Money, Africell Money or QMoney.

3
00:00:30,099 --> 00:00:50,435
The platform keeps a small fee from every payment, and an organization admin must
agree to it first. If you try to save without ticking the box, you are asked to agree.
Tick it and save, and payments are on. If you change a setting later, the box clears,
and you tick it again before saving.

4
00:00:51,035 --> 00:01:01,673
The Payments tab of the program lists every payment, who paid, how they paid, and its
status. Paid, cancelled and waiting payments are all recorded.

5
00:01:02,273 --> 00:01:20,140
All the money goes to your payment fund. Available is what you can withdraw now. On
hold is money still inside the short waiting time after a payment. Below, you can see
the total received all time, the total after the platform fee, and the total after
refunds.

6
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:42,286
To withdraw, first add a withdrawal account, a mobile money number or a bank account,
and confirm with your password. A new account can be used after a short waiting time.
Then press Withdraw, choose the account and the amount, and confirm with your
password. Large withdrawals wait for approval from the platform team.

7
00:01:42,886 --> 00:01:59,063
If you want your money sent on straight away, turn on Automatic withdrawal. Choose an
account and confirm with your password. From then on, each successful payment is sent
to that account with no waiting time, and the platform fee is still taken.

8
00:01:59,663 --> 00:02:11,891
Everything is recorded. The Withdrawals table shows each withdrawal and its status,
and Money in and out lists every payment received, every fee and every withdrawal,
newest first.

9
00:02:12,491 --> 00:02:31,152
The platform team sees every organization's totals: money paid in, fees, refunds,
withdrawals, and what is left in each fund. For each organization they can also set
the platform fee, the waiting time before money can be withdrawn, and when withdrawals
switch on.

10
00:02:31,752 --> 00:02:37,411
That is how payments work in NTSOne. Use this video as your guide.
